{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions","id":1299628,"title":"62 Kiths Converted to 2E (Olivia Hill Kith Conversions)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-25T09:50:28-07:00","id":1299628,"title":"62 Kiths Converted to 2E (Olivia Hill Kith Conversions)","content":"So, this is a thing. Before I get into it, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eyi9aImrH4RUtJvuiTTc7G5cspiXW19CidUlnks4YJc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here's the good stuff.</a><br /> Of note, <b>all of the fluff and some of the mechanics </b><b>use the verbiage from the playtest documents - I did not write these and it is not a wholly original product.</b><br /> <br /> I love Second Edition Changeling, and I also love having huge amounts of character options. When I saw that the number of Kiths in the release version of changeling was vastly lower than what we saw in the previews of Olivia's version, I was a little disappointed, but it made a kind of sense. Thankfully, 2E included rules for creating new Kiths, and Olivia's work certainly laid plenty of groundwork for inspiration. I converted my first one (Brewer) several months ago, but over the past few days I sat down and decided to just go ahead and convert them all. This has been quite a process.<br /> <br /> Things I learned:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The Kith creation guidelines are solid, but following them <i>too</i> rigidly leads to everything feeling same-y. When I revisit this again, I'll probably make some more unique takes on things.</li> <li>Olivia Hill's product had too many Kiths. So many of them were basically 'the same concept, but recycled in this slightly different manner' and could really have just been flavor adjustments of each other, instead of wholly new Kiths. Several also felt like particular expressions of the Elemental Seeming that didn't need to be a Kith in the first place. That said, I did convert each of them as their own 'Thing' and did my best to differentiate their Blessings and Trickeries to make differences between similar Kiths more meaningful.</li> <li>Similarly, some of the Kiths in the original product had mechanics in their blessing that were essentially 'like this other Kith's blessing, but better'. I tried to eliminate that, but as there was a <i>lot</i> of overlap, I'm sure there are several instances where I failed.</li> </ol>Things I would love feedback on:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Wyrd Scaling - I tried to include a lot of this so that the Trickeries would feel useful throughout the game. It might be too much, or (my main concern) it might lead to a lot of these being too underwhelming early game. If you test any of these out in actual play experience, please let me know what you think.</li> <li>Blessings - There are 62 Kiths and only 24 skills, but the vast majority of Blessings only benefit a small subset of skills, and many skills aren't represented here at all. I would love some ideas to build variety in represented skills here, without sacrificing the integrity of the Kiths in question.</li> </ol>That's about it - please pass along any feedback here (just try to remain constructive).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:56:58-07:00","id":1299636,"title":"","content":"Notes on my general design philosophy here (I did not succeed at hitting every point with every Kith):<br /> <br /> 1) Passives and Stat modifiers are boring when there's no element of choice involved - Trickeries should primarily expand the available options of the player, not <i>just</i> move dots on their sheet.<br /> 2) Every Trickery should be cool enough to inspire character concepts on its own, not simply serve to supplement existing concepts.<br /> 3) The rules used for each Trickery should be clear and concise, with clarity taking priority.<br /> 4) Each Kith should have access to abilities that make them meaningfully different from other, similar ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:57:15-07:00","id":1299655,"title":"","content":"I'm confused? kiths like True friend are already in 2nd edition. are these supposed to be alternate take","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T11:09:58-07:00","id":1299658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1299655#post1299655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused? kiths like True friend are already in 2nd edition. are these supposed to be alternate take</div> </div> </div> </div>The only Kiths in 2nd Edition are:<br /> Artist, Bright One, Chatelaine, Gristlegrinder, Helldiver, Hunterheart, Leechfinger, Mirrorskin, Nightsinger, Notary, Playmate, and Snowskin.<br /> <br /> All of the Kiths in this google document were <i>going</i> to be in Olivia's version of 2E, and can still be found in the playtest drafts. What I've done is take those and convert them to versions that are mechanically compatible with the <i>released</i> version of 2E, where Kiths work very differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  Clarity 03-25-2019, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T11:58:30-07:00","id":1299675,"title":"","content":"ahh ok. thanks!<br /> <br /> EDIT: I really like your far Walker and troll kith!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-25-2019, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T14:37:06-07:00","id":1299736,"title":"","content":"You are doing God's work!<br /> <br /> From a cursory glance, my first comment is that Metalflesh's Kith Blessing and Trickery would be better suited for a Hacker themed Kith. Here is how I would do it.<br /> <br /> Kith Blessing: When rolling Intimidation through sheer endurance of body and mind, the Metalflesh gains an Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> <br /> Trickery: By spending 1 Glamour, the Metalflesh may roll [highest between Stamina and Resolve] + Intimidation to not be affected by a Mental or Physical Tilts equal to Successes for a number of turns equal to Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-25-2019, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T14:40:52-07:00","id":1299738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1299736#post1299736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a cursory glance, my first comment is that Metalflesh's Kith Blessing and Trickery would be better suited for a Hacker themed Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely accurate. They were one of the Kiths where their blessing was, essentially 'this other Kith, but worse' so I tried to do something different, and ended up with something totally out of theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1299736#post1299736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kith Blessing: When rolling Intimidation through sheer endurance of body and mind, the Metalflesh gains an Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> <br /> Trickery: By spending 1 Glamour, the Metalflesh may roll Stamina + Intimidation to not be affected by a Mental or Physical Tilts equal to Successes for a number of turns equal to Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mind if I copy this over wholesale into the document?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T14:44:59-07:00","id":1299740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1299738#post1299738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mind if I copy this over wholesale into the document?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not at all, I'm quite flattered actually. But if you don't mind, could you change the dice pool to [highest between Stamina and Resolve] + Intimidation? They are about endurance of body and mind, after all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T15:10:20-07:00","id":1300112,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. I don't think you can get an Exceptional Success on combat rolls like you mentioned for Razorhand and Bloodbrute. You just do more damage, I believe.<br /> <br /> Also, I am pretty sure Razorhand is supposed to use Weaponry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-26-2019, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T15:17:37-07:00","id":1300118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1300112#post1300112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something. I don't think you can get an Exceptional Success on combat rolls like you mentioned for Razorhand and Bloodbrute. You just do more damage, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no unique special effect for Exceptional Success on attack rolls, but the Gristlegrinder blessing specifically applies to grappling attempts and there's no special exception stated for the common rolls in the Violence section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T15:23:38-07:00","id":1300121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1300112#post1300112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something. I don't think you can get an Exceptional Success on combat rolls like you mentioned for Razorhand and Bloodbrute. You just do more damage, I believe.<br /> <br /> Also, I am pretty sure Razorhand is supposed to use Weaponry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says combat rolls <i>can't</i> get Exceptional Success. There's just no example results for combat rolls just like almost all other mundane actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T15:25:42-07:00","id":1300123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1300121#post1300121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing says combat rolls <i>can't</i> get Exceptional Success. There's just no example results for combat rolls just like almost all other mundane actions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, with the exception of grappling, which allows you to act out two (different) grappling maneuvers in one action if you manage to get an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T18:37:39-07:00","id":1300161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1300121#post1300121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing says combat rolls <i>can't</i> get Exceptional Success. There's just no example results for combat rolls just like almost all other mundane actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've either been handing out Steadfast or allowing the player to apply a weapon appropriate tilt to the target; I've also thought about allowing such an attack to bypass or damage armor, but am on the fence about it. Exceptional successes on combat rolls don't come up too often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T08:15:14-07:00","id":1300847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1300112#post1300112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something. I don't think you can get an Exceptional Success on combat rolls like you mentioned for Razorhand and Bloodbrute.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's never called out that you can't, so the standard guidelines for exceptional success would apply - bringing a Condition into play. At my table, we allow Tilts in combat as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1300112#post1300112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I am pretty sure Razorhand is supposed to use Weaponry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is this? They have natural weapons, and all other instances of natural weaponry in CofD 2E use Brawl.<br /> I'm not disagreeing with you, I think I'm just missing context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T20:30:26-07:00","id":1303701,"title":"","content":"One Kith I noticed that was missing from the list was the Windwing Beast Kith from 1st Edition, I was wondering how exactly one would convert that Kith to 2nd Edition? <br /> I have included my attempt at conversion please offer any feedback you might have;considering I have little experience with this I used the first part of the Hunterheart Skill bonus and added the Windwing kith blessing from 1st edition as it was written. <br /> Choose either Investigation or Sur\u00advival. When the Windwing uses the chosen Skill to track down creatures from Faerie, achieving three suc\u00adcesses counts as an exceptional success.Gift of Flight: A Windwing may spend a point of Glamour to glide in the air for up to one minute per point Wyrd; he cannot gain altitude without appropriate updrafts, but may move at his normal Speed. In addition, a Windwing takes only one point of bashing damage for every 15 yards fallen, and begins to take lethal damage only if he falls more than 150 yards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T21:45:44-07:00","id":1303711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1303701#post1303701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Kith I noticed that was missing from the list was the Windwing Beast Kith from 1st Edition, I was wondering how exactly one would convert that Kith to 2nd Edition? <br /> I have included my attempt at conversion please offer any feedback you might have;considering I have little experience with this I used the first part of the Hunterheart Skill bonus and added the Windwing kith blessing from 1st edition as it was written. <br /> Choose either Investigation or Sur*vival. When the Windwing uses the chosen Skill to track down creatures from Faerie, achieving three suc*cesses counts as an exceptional success.Gift of Flight: A Windwing may spend a point of Glamour to glide in the air for up to one minute per point Wyrd; he cannot gain altitude without appropriate updrafts, but may move at his normal Speed. In addition, a Windwing takes only one point of bashing damage for every 15 yards fallen, and begins to take lethal damage only if he falls more than 150 yards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I might have begun working on the Windwing conversion for the other thread, and then never posted it up. I\u2019ll check my files tomorrow to see if it\u2019s hanging around, and if so, I\u2019ll post it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T06:35:03-07:00","id":1303766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1303701#post1303701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Kith I noticed that was missing from the list was the Windwing Beast Kith from 1st Edition, I was wondering how exactly one would convert that Kith to 2nd Edition?<br /> I have included my attempt at conversion please offer any feedback you might have;considering I have little experience with this I used the first part of the Hunterheart Skill bonus and added the Windwing kith blessing from 1st edition as it was written.<br /> Choose either Investigation or Sur*vival. When the Windwing uses the chosen Skill to track down creatures from Faerie, achieving three suc*cesses counts as an exceptional success.Gift of Flight: A Windwing may spend a point of Glamour to glide in the air for up to one minute per point Wyrd; he cannot gain altitude without appropriate updrafts, but may move at his normal Speed. In addition, a Windwing takes only one point of bashing damage for every 15 yards fallen, and begins to take lethal damage only if he falls more than 150 yards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I checked my notes. I don't have their full conversion finished, but I did have their kith blessing. For convenience, I'll post it here:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Kith Blessing: </b>When the Windwing uses Survival while airborne for foraging, hunting, or navigation, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Sky\u2019s Freedom: </i>By spending a point of Glamour and rolling Stamina + Athletics, a Windwing is able to take to the sky. The Windwing is able to fly at twice their Speed for one minute for each success rolled, and is able to use their Defense against Firearms while airborne. This time is increased to five minutes for each success rolled while in the Hedge, although those skies often have their own complications. After the flight duration lapses, the Windwing becomes fatigued, gliding gently to the ground. The character must rest for a turn before using this Blessing again.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T15:06:57-07:00","id":1303836,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the Windwing Kith Blessing Conversion, I am looking forward to reading the rest of the conversion once you get it completed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T19:43:30-08:00","id":1354956,"title":"","content":"My Summer King is a fire elemental based on the mythical salamander and I decided that his Keeper decided to use him as the fire in a weapons forge used by the Keepers other changelings. That being said I was wondering if he would fit under the Ifrit or Fireheart kiths found within the Olivia Hill Kith conversions list?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T04:45:34-08:00","id":1354980,"title":"","content":"Fire-as-weapon is typically more the Ifrit's domain; Firehearts are more metaphorically bright, ie quick witted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T07:47:44-08:00","id":1355005,"title":"","content":"So are you advising me to leave him as a kithless elemental or if I did decide to give him a kith make him a maker or a smith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T09:56:25-08:00","id":1356314,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if you guys could help me out with converting the Shadowsoul kith to 2nd Edition? I have included what I have thus far as well as the text from the Shadowsoul entry in Winter Masques.<ul><li>Shadowsoul<ul><li>1<sup>st</sup> Edition Wording:<ul><li><i>Shadowsoul </i>\u2014 The antithesis of the Bright Ones, these fae are the most beautiful chosen of the nigh. Their beauty comes from the darkness they swathe themselves in rather than the light they radiate. They were the favored concubines, adornments and hand-maidens to nocturnal Keepers, and are distant cousins to the Darklings.</li> <li>The Shadowsoul\u2019s blessing is the <b>Unnatural Chill</b>: the player gains a bonus to Intimidation rolls equal to her Wyrd, and receives the benefit of the 9 again rule to Subterfuge rolls. In addition, she may purchase Contracts of Darkness as affinity Contracts.</li> </ul></li> <li>Purpose (Primary Category)<ul><li>Handmaiden (Social)</li> </ul></li> <li>Benefits<ul><li>Skill (Intimidation)<ul><li>Exceptional Success with 3 Successes<ul><li>When using Intimidation for social maneuvering.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Trickery<ul><li>Spend point of Glamour and make Presence + Intimidation roll<ul><li>Unnatural Chill: Gains a bonus to Intimidation roll equal to her Wyrd.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T00:48:04-08:00","id":1356450,"title":"","content":"For the Shadowsouled, I would do it as a Presence + Manipulation roll. On a successful roll, you inflict the spooked condition on your target","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T02:05:21-08:00","id":1356455,"title":"","content":"The update of it I know (not my own, linked to me by a friend) has these stats:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadowsoul:<br /> <br /> When the Shadowsoul uses Subterfuge to obfuscate their desires and goals, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success. <br /> <br /> Shroud: A Shadowsoul carries a palpable gloom, dimming sources of illumination, though the Mask normally prevents mortals from seeing it. She can spend a point of Glamour to cast the immediate area in a chilling shadow, and one Glamour every turn thereafter to maintain it; the Mask does not obscure this darkness. Each turn the Shadowsoul uses this blessing, she applies the Poor Light Tilt to the area, and her enemies take a point of bashing damage from supernatural darkness. This darkness smothers mundane light sources and supernatural sources of light trigger a Clash of Wills. In addition, the Shadowsoul can see normally in poor lighting, up to and including pitch darkness. </div> </div> </div>I find this works well for it being an antithesis of the Bright One Kith","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T09:14:01-08:00","id":1358886,"title":"","content":"Jakodite, Would the following be an accurate written description of the example you gave me?<ul><li>Benefits<ul><li>Skill (Intimidation)<ul><li>Exceptional Success with 3 Successes<ul><li>When using Intimidation for social maneuvering.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Trickery<ul><li>Spend point of Glamour and make Presence + Manipulation roll<ul><li>Unnatural Chill: Inflicts the spooked condition on the target with a successful Presence + Manipulation roll and spending a point of Glamour.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T23:08:26-07:00","id":1385198,"title":"","content":"I've made some minor updates to the document.<br /> <br /> I didn't receive much feedback the first time around, but now that this document has circulated fairly widely, I'm curious if anyone that's tried these out in actual play has feedback of the sort requested in the OP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:51:48-07:00","id":1385521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1385198#post1385198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made some minor updates to the document.<br /> <br /> I didn't receive much feedback the first time around, but now that this document has circulated fairly widely, I'm curious if anyone that's tried these out in actual play has feedback of the sort requested in the OP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops. Sorry for not commenting. I Always used this list. It helped some of my players to find more interesting options. I personally like the brewer kith. But i find the toxicity a little too high because of the addition of the sucesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T03:27:23-07:00","id":1385570,"title":"","content":"This is awesome, the number of Kiths in the core book did seem a little sparse. i do have a question regarding the Nix though. <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kith Blessing: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Nix makes Athletics rolls related to swimming or water sports, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Siren\u2019s Lure: </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Nix can breathe water as easily as air. </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The changeling may spend a point of Glamour and roll Presence + Expression to ignore social penalties or Resistance up to the rolled successes plus Wyrd for the scene. This includes penalties from Forcing Doors in Social Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> Are Nix meant to be good in the water, or good in social encounters, because it looks like they start out as the former then somehow change to the later. I mean, what does ignoring social penalties have to do with being able to breathe water as easily as air. There was a Kith (can't remember what it was called) that could breathe underwater, and grant their water breathing to others. Maybe that would be better for the Nix? Or maybe make a third water-based Kith for the water-breathing ability?</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T18:22:54-07:00","id":1388514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1299628-62-kiths-converted-to-2e-olivia-hill-kith-conversions?p=1385570#post1385570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Nix meant to be good in the water, or good in social encounters, because it looks like they start out as the former then somehow change to the later. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good question - here's the original, pre-conversion version from the 2E Playtest:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blessing:\u200bA nix can breathe water as easily as air and adds +2 to all swimming rolls. If she spends a point of Glamour and speaks, she adds her Wyrd to all Persuasion or vocal Expression rolls for the scene and listeners subtract the nix\u2019s Wyrd from all Wits + Composure rolls to notice anything except the changeling. </div> </div> </div>So, the answer would appear to be both - I believe it's meant to be a play on the tropes of a water-dwelling creature that's good at luring people to their deaths, or at the very least, fatally distracting them. I tried to stay true to the original design with most of these conversions, though avoiding rehashing the same thing 30 different ways took priority (and that still happened, occasionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T17:44:04-07:00","id":1493546,"title":"","content":"Thank you for doing this, @Inodiv. Truly, you are doing <s>God's</s> the Wyrd's work. I too was excited when I learned that 2e would canonize my houserule that Kiths and Seemings can be mixed freely, but very disappointed to learn at how paltry few Kiths were included in the 2e corebook. Thanks to you, I now have dozens of snazzy new options to choose from when I'm building new characters or NPCs. Thank you again! \ud83d\ude47\u200d\u2642\ufe0f\ud83d\ude47\u200d\u2642\ufe0f\ud83d\ude47\u200d\u2642\ufe0f","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T10:02:23-07:00","id":1493636,"title":"","content":"Some good stuff there on the Darklings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.c